00:03:01.520 --> 00:03:07.540
technical, a long-term grassland experiment examined multiple global change factors together.

00:03:08.180 --> 00:03:14.080
Elevated temperature and elevated CO2 together raised total below ground carbon allocation as the

00:03:14.080 --> 00:03:20.160
experiment progressed through time. Drought conditions and nitrogen addition each altered the size of

00:03:20.160 --> 00:03:26.000
that increase. The combined interactions produce larger effects on carbon allocation than single

00:03:26.000 --> 00:03:32.140
factor changes alone. Results point to the need for updated soil carbon models that incorporate

00:03:32.140 --> 00:03:39.080
interacting drivers rather than isolated variables. Such models feed directly into risk assessments

00:03:39.080 --> 00:03:47.640
and site closure criteria applied under provincial frameworks such as BC, CSR, and Alberta EPEA.

00:03:48.180 --> 00:03:54.560
In industry and practice, federal funding supports deployment of a renewable microgrid serving remote

00:03:54.560 --> 00:04:01.520
