00:05:00.520 --> 00:05:07.000
Under Ontario EPA approvals, the ministry retains discretion to require combined effects modeling

00:05:07.540 --> 00:05:14.060
even when individual source contributions fall below screening thresholds. Experience practitioners

00:05:14.060 --> 00:05:20.740
recognize that residential receptors within 500 meters often drive the need for refined dispersion runs

00:05:20.740 --> 00:05:26.040
using site-specific meteorological data rather than conservative defaults.

00:05:26.460 --> 00:05:31.680
Regulators increasingly expect explicit justification for excluding nearby sources,

00:05:32.160 --> 00:05:36.320
particularly when public correspondence has already highlighted health concerns.

00:05:37.160 --> 00:05:42.540
The mistake I see most often is assuming that meeting individual source emission limits

00:05:42.540 --> 00:05:49.900
satisfies the cumulative obligation. The fix is to document the rationale for source inclusion or

00:05:49.900 --> 00:05:56.540
exclusion in the initial modeling plan submitted with the application. If you are working on industrial

